-- A value is a normal form — the companion to progress, proved in Thena's
-- surface language.
--
-- LOAD AFTER canonical.thena AND progress.thena. Thena has no module imports;
-- globals declared by one module are in scope for the next.
--
-- Progress says a well-typed term is a value OR it takes a step. Nothing said
-- those were exclusive, and this does: a value takes no step at all, well typed
-- or not. Together they say the disjunction progress returns is a real case
-- split rather than a possibly-overlapping pair.
--
-- EVERY PROOF HERE IS A SPLIT, and three of them have no cases at all. Every
-- constructor of Step has `ifthen`, `succ`, `pred` or `iszero` at its source,
-- so against `true`, `false` or `zero` every method is closed by a conflicting
-- equation and there is nothing left to answer. This file used to write out all
-- ten methods of `elim Step` for each of those three, and discharge each one
-- with `absurd` and `noConfusionTerm`.
--
-- THE CASE THAT IS NOT IMMEDIATE IS `succ`, where the step must be a congruence
-- and the induction hypothesis is what kills it — and the hypothesis IS the
-- recursive call `nvNoStep c1 nn a2 sr`. Nothing binds a hypothesis and nothing
-- transports along an equation.
--
-- THE WHOLE STATEMENT IS INTRODUCED AT THE TOP, `\ t n u s ->`, which is what a
-- student writes. The split on `n` refines the index `t`, so it generalises the
-- premises that mention it — `u` and `s` — and both names go on meaning the
-- refined thing inside the arm. Which positions were copied is elaboration's
-- business and not the author's.
--
-- THE FIVE STATEMENTS ARE LEVEL-POLYMORPHIC NOW, where they used to be at level
-- 0. A declared type's level is generalised when nothing pins it, and nothing
-- here passes `Empty` to `absurd` any more.

module Normal where

trueNoStep : forall (u : Term) (s : Step true u) -> Empty
trueNoStep = \ u s -> case s of { }

falseNoStep : forall (u : Term) (s : Step false u) -> Empty
falseNoStep = \ u s -> case s of { }

zeroNoStep : forall (u : Term) (s : Step zero u) -> Empty
zeroNoStep = \ u s -> case s of { }

nvNoStep : forall (t : Term) (n : NV t) (u : Term) (s : Step t u) -> Empty
nvNoStep = \ t n u s -> induction n of
  { nvZero -> zeroNoStep u s
  ; nvSucc c1 nn -> case s of { eSucc a1 a2 sr -> nvNoStep c1 nn a2 sr } }

valueNoStep : forall (v : Term) (p : Value v) (u : Term) (s : Step v u) -> Empty
valueNoStep = \ v p u s -> case p of
  { vTrue -> trueNoStep u s
  ; vFalse -> falseNoStep u s
  ; vNat c1 nn -> nvNoStep c1 nn u s }
